# Breadcrumb

Shows the path to the current page as a trail of links. Compose it from `Breadcrumb`, `BreadcrumbList`, `BreadcrumbItem`, `BreadcrumbLink`, `BreadcrumbPage`, `BreadcrumbSeparator`, and `BreadcrumbEllipsis`.

<Demo />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<script lang="ts">
	import { Breadcrumb, BreadcrumbList, BreadcrumbItem, BreadcrumbLink, BreadcrumbPage, BreadcrumbSeparator } from "#lib/components/ui/breadcrumb/index.js";
</script>

<Breadcrumb>
	<BreadcrumbList>
		<BreadcrumbItem><BreadcrumbLink href="/">Home</BreadcrumbLink></BreadcrumbItem>
		<BreadcrumbSeparator />
		<BreadcrumbItem><BreadcrumbLink href="/docs/components">Components</BreadcrumbLink></BreadcrumbItem>
		<BreadcrumbSeparator />
		<BreadcrumbItem><BreadcrumbPage>Breadcrumb</BreadcrumbPage></BreadcrumbItem>
	</BreadcrumbList>
</Breadcrumb>
```

## Installation

```pm
npx remote0 add https://plainsv.com/r/breadcrumb.json
```

## Anatomy

`Breadcrumb` renders a `nav` with `aria-label="breadcrumb"` and sets the size of its parts. `BreadcrumbList` renders an `ol` that wraps onto more lines when it runs out of room. Each `BreadcrumbItem` renders an `li` that holds a `BreadcrumbLink`, a `BreadcrumbPage`, or a `BreadcrumbEllipsis`.

`BreadcrumbLink` renders a plain `a`, so SvelteKit handles it as client-side navigation. `BreadcrumbPage` marks the last step with `aria-current="page"` and is not clickable. `BreadcrumbSeparator` renders an `li` that is hidden from screen readers, since the list already announces each step.

## Separator

Pass children to `BreadcrumbSeparator` to replace the default chevron, such as with another icon or text.

<Demo section="separator" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<script lang="ts">
	import { BreadcrumbSeparator } from "#lib/components/ui/breadcrumb/index.js";
	import { SlashIcon } from "@lucide/svelte";
</script>

<BreadcrumbSeparator><SlashIcon /></BreadcrumbSeparator>
```

## Dropdown

Place a `DropdownMenu` inside a `BreadcrumbItem` to let a step open a menu, such as of its sibling pages. Use the `trigger` snippet to render a bare button that matches the links.

<Demo section="dropdown" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<script lang="ts">
	import { Breadcrumb, BreadcrumbList, BreadcrumbItem, BreadcrumbLink, BreadcrumbPage, BreadcrumbSeparator } from "#lib/components/ui/breadcrumb/index.js";
	import { DropdownMenu, DropdownMenuTrigger, DropdownMenuContent, DropdownMenuItem } from "#lib/components/ui/dropdown-menu/index.js";
</script>

<Breadcrumb>
	<BreadcrumbList>
		<BreadcrumbItem><BreadcrumbLink href="/">Home</BreadcrumbLink></BreadcrumbItem>
		<BreadcrumbSeparator />
		<BreadcrumbItem>
			<DropdownMenu size="lg">
				<DropdownMenuTrigger>
					{#snippet trigger({ props })}
						<button class="menuTrigger" {...props}>Components</button>
					{/snippet}
				</DropdownMenuTrigger>
				<DropdownMenuContent>
					<DropdownMenuItem>Documentation</DropdownMenuItem>
					<DropdownMenuItem>Themes</DropdownMenuItem>
					<DropdownMenuItem>GitHub</DropdownMenuItem>
				</DropdownMenuContent>
			</DropdownMenu>
		</BreadcrumbItem>
		<BreadcrumbSeparator />
		<BreadcrumbItem><BreadcrumbPage>Breadcrumb</BreadcrumbPage></BreadcrumbItem>
	</BreadcrumbList>
</Breadcrumb>
```

## Collapsed

Use `BreadcrumbEllipsis` in place of the middle items when the trail is long.

<Demo section="collapsed" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<Breadcrumb>
	<BreadcrumbList>
		<BreadcrumbItem><BreadcrumbLink href="/">Home</BreadcrumbLink></BreadcrumbItem>
		<BreadcrumbSeparator />
		<BreadcrumbItem><BreadcrumbEllipsis /></BreadcrumbItem>
		<BreadcrumbSeparator />
		<BreadcrumbItem><BreadcrumbLink href="/docs/components">Components</BreadcrumbLink></BreadcrumbItem>
		<BreadcrumbSeparator />
		<BreadcrumbItem><BreadcrumbPage>Breadcrumb</BreadcrumbPage></BreadcrumbItem>
	</BreadcrumbList>
</Breadcrumb>
```

To list the collapsed items in a menu, as in the preview at the top of this page, wrap the ellipsis in a ghost icon `Button`. The ellipsis is hidden from screen readers, so give the button an `aria-label` such as `Show more pages`.

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<script lang="ts">
	import { BreadcrumbItem, BreadcrumbEllipsis } from "#lib/components/ui/breadcrumb/index.js";
	import { DropdownMenu, DropdownMenuTrigger, DropdownMenuContent, DropdownMenuItem } from "#lib/components/ui/dropdown-menu/index.js";
	import { Button } from "#lib/components/ui/button/index.js";
</script>

<BreadcrumbItem>
	<DropdownMenu size="lg">
		<DropdownMenuTrigger>
			{#snippet trigger({ props })}
				<Button variant="ghost" size="icon-sm" aria-label="Show more pages" {...props}><BreadcrumbEllipsis /></Button>
			{/snippet}
		</DropdownMenuTrigger>
		<DropdownMenuContent>
			<DropdownMenuItem>Documentation</DropdownMenuItem>
			<DropdownMenuItem>Themes</DropdownMenuItem>
			<DropdownMenuItem>GitHub</DropdownMenuItem>
		</DropdownMenuContent>
	</DropdownMenu>
</BreadcrumbItem>
```

## Icons

Place an icon before or after the text of a `BreadcrumbLink` or `BreadcrumbPage`. Icons scale with the size.

<Demo section="icons" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<script lang="ts">
	import { BreadcrumbLink } from "#lib/components/ui/breadcrumb/index.js";
	import { HouseIcon } from "@lucide/svelte";
</script>

<BreadcrumbLink href="/"><HouseIcon />Home</BreadcrumbLink>
```

## Sizes

Set `size` on `Breadcrumb` to `xs`, `sm`, `md`, or `lg`. The default is `md`, and the text, gap, and icons follow the size.

<Demo section="sizes" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<Breadcrumb size="sm">...</Breadcrumb>
```

## API

Each part extends the native attributes of the element it renders: `nav`, `ol`, `li`, `a`, and `span`. Extra attributes pass through to each element.

```ts title="index.ts"
interface Props extends CompPropsWithChild<"nav"> {
	/** Text, gap, and icon size on the shared scale; defaults to `md` */
	size?: UiSize;
}

interface ListProps extends CompPropsWithChild<"ol"> {}

interface ItemProps extends CompPropsWithChild<"li"> {}

interface LinkProps extends CompPropsWithChild<"a"> {}

interface PageProps extends CompPropsWithChild<"span"> {}

interface SeparatorProps extends CompProps<"li"> {
	/** Custom divider content in place of the chevron */
	children?: Snippet;
}

interface EllipsisProps extends CompProps<"span"> {}
```
